    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Per-method decorators generate a single test that loops for each test parameter, so the test needs to emit a single, aggregated status for test results of all parameters. I think the current logic is to treat skip as success (with stdout).\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/cupy/cupy/blob/8ddb02d9f75f22ba0b17b83545124aed4d11d2ec/cupy/testing/_loops.py#L837-L851",
